Module options for BusyBox's modprobe (modprobe-small reads /etc/modules/NAME when it loads module NAME).
asus_wmi (1.4.4): fnlock_default=0. The driver otherwise starts with Fn lock on, so F1-F12 send F1-F12 and the
volume and brightness keys need Fn; Windows ships these laptops the other way round (the ASUS Vivobook Go: F1 mute,
F2/F3 volume, F4/F5 brightness without Fn). Fn+Esc still switches it.
rtw88_pci (1.5.6): disable_aspm=1. The PCIe link power saving (ASPM) of Realtek's rtw88 Wi-Fi chips (the RTL8821CE of
the ASUS Vivobook Go, the RTL8822CE and RTL8822BE) is a known cause of dropped Wi-Fi connections; wifi.sh also sets it
for a driver already loaded.
